# TitanLLPS — Liquid-Liquid Phase Separation Analysis (Martini CG)

Adds a new `TitanLLPS` module that analyses LLPS condensate formation from Martini coarse-grained trajectories. It detects chain contacts via a cell-list (O(N)), computes GCC fraction, Rg, density, C(t) autocorrelation, and degree distribution frame by frame, then exports Python-friendly output files.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Chain topology assumption**: The chain-to-bead map is built from `molecule_trackers` (per-molecule bead-index lists). The code must be wired in [impl_engine.cpp](file:///c:/Users/ADMIN/OneDrive/Documents/antigravity/elec_vdw/impl_engine.cpp) at the point where `molecule_trackers` is already populated (after Martini topology parsing). Please confirm that `molecule_trackers` refers to the `Multi_MOL::info` vector grouped by chain.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Coordinate units in traj**: GROMACS XTC/TRR positions are in **nm** already after gmxtraj conversion. The `traj.box` from gmxtraj is also nm. This assumption is used throughout — please confirm.

> [!NOTE]
> **Contact map** (`-llps-contacts`) is opt-in because it requires O(N_res²) RAM. Omit for large systems.

