### Core module

#### [NEW] [titan_llps.h](file:///c:/Users/ADMIN/OneDrive/Documents/antigravity/elec_vdw/titan_llps.h)
```
Structs:
  LLPSFrameResult  — per-frame snapshot (gcc_fraction, gcc_size, gcc_rg_nm,
                      mean_degree, density_dense, density_dilute)
  LLPSResult       — full trajectory results + C(t) vector + contact_freq

class TitanLLPS:
  Private data:
    chain_beads_[n_chains][n_beads_per_chain]   — bead index map
    bb_bead_per_chain_[n_chains]                — backbone bead (first BB/BB1)
    adj_snapshots_[frame]                       — bit-packed uint64_t (N²/64)
    percolation_frame_                           — first frame with f > thr
    contact_freq_[res_i][res_j]                 — float accumulator (opt-in)
    sticker_mask_[n_atoms]                      — bool: is this bead a sticker?

  Public API:
    TitanLLPS(n_chains, chain_beads, r_cut_nm, perc_thr, contacts_on)
    void process_frame(const float* pos, const float box[3][3],
                       float time_ns, int frame_idx)
    void finalize(int n_threads, int max_lag_frames)
    void export_results(const info&, std::fstream&) const
    const LLPSResult& result() const
```

#### [NEW] [titan_llps.cpp](file:///c:/Users/ADMIN/OneDrive/Documents/antigravity/elec_vdw/titan_llps.cpp)

**process_frame() — cell-list O(N), called in hot loop:**
1. Build cell-grid: `cell_size = r_cut`, `nx = floor(box_x / cell_size)`, etc.
2. Assign each bead to cell [(ix, iy, iz)](file:///c:/Users/ADMIN/OneDrive/Documents/antigravity/elec_vdw/info.h#8-196).
3. For each bead, check 27 neighbor cells; compute PBC-minimum-image distance to each candidate bead.
4. If `d < r_cut` and `chain_i ≠ chain_j`: mark contact pair [(min, max)](file:///c:/Users/ADMIN/OneDrive/Documents/antigravity/elec_vdw/info.h#8-196).
5. Run Union-Find on unique chain-pairs → GCC size, `gcc_fraction`.
6. Compute GCC Rg using BB beads only (PBC-corrected centroid).
7. Compute `density_dense`, `density_dilute` (sphere approx Rg³).
8. Compute `mean_degree = 2 * n_edges / n_chains`.
9. Store bit-packed adjacency (if `percolation_frame_ == -1` or C(t) needed).
10. If `contacts_on_`: accumulate `contact_freq_` for sticker beads.
11. Push `LLPSFrameResult` to `result_.frames`.

**finalize() — called once after all frames, parallelized:**
- C(t) = bitwise XOR + AND + popcount over lag × time loop (parallelized across lags via `std::thread`).
- Fit `τ` via integral of C(t) to 1/e crossing.
- Compute P(k) histogram mean and std across frames.
- Normalize `contact_freq_` by [n_frames](file:///c:/Users/ADMIN/OneDrive/Documents/antigravity/elec_vdw/titan_msm.h#94-96).
- Set `result_.is_percolated`, `result_.percolation_time_ns`.

**export_results():**
- `llps_timeseries.dat`: one row per frame.
- `llps_autocorr.dat`: lag_ns, C(t).
- `llps_degree_dist.dat`: k, P(k)_mean, P(k)_std.
- `llps_contact_map.dat`: N_res × N_res matrix (if contacts enabled).
- `llps_summary.dat`: percolated, tau_ns, percolation_time_ns, mean_gcc_rg_nm.

